  "description": "Original #374 NRegress omission: all retained premises hold while the absolute unmoved-mover conclusion fails. The omitted premise is refuted by composition with the existing theorem. The unchanged interpretation also satisfies motion-in-the-moved and every mover being in act, jointly with the existing potency and non-simultaneity evaluations. Its actual two-cycle uses different respects (a moves b in k, b moves a in h), so same-respect consecutive-edge exclusion is compatible with a cycle and absence of a globally unmoved mover. Well-foundedness of MovesAsMoved is a separate violated premise, not merely a prohibition of distinct-node infinite chains.",
